! A final group that stops in the middle of itself.
!
! IDF closes an object with a semicolon wherever the author stops, so the last group of an
! extensible object can carry fewer fields than the group is wide. Nothing marks that in
! the file: the reader has to notice the group ran out. "Truncated Equipment List" stops
! after the first field of a two-field group, and "Truncated Annual Table" writes one whole
! three-field group and then stops after the second field of the next one.
!
! This is not the blank-slot hazard. No comma stands for a missing value here; the fields
! are simply not in the file.

Version,
  26.1;

Building,
  Minimal Building;

GlobalGeometryRules,
  UpperLeftCorner,
  Counterclockwise,
  Relative;

PlantEquipmentList,
  Truncated Equipment List,
  Pump:ConstantSpeed;

Output:Table:Annual,
  Truncated Annual Table,
  Zone One,
  Table Schedule,
  Zone Air Temperature,
  SumOrAverage,
  2,
  Zone Air Humidity Ratio,
  Maximum;
